{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>עוצו.</b> The meaning: all that you counsel against Jerusalem, the counsel shall not stand. Now עוצו is from the two apparent ones [i.e., a plural form], and R. Moses the Kohen, of blessed memory, said that it is deficient in yod, and it ought to have been יעוצו, like זכורו (Nehemiah 4:8):" "<b>כי עמנו אל.</b> This is the meaning of the name of the prophet's son:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The phrase 'from the two apparent ones' refers to Ibn Ezra's grammatical analysis of the form; translated literally as the original is terse and technical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:48.408341032Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}